{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscardingTaskGroup"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To create a discarding task group,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call the ","type":"text"},{"code":"withDiscardingTaskGroup(returning:body:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t use a task group from outside the task where you created it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In most cases,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Swift type system prevents a task group from escaping like that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because adding a child task to a task group is a mutating operation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and mutation operations can’t be performed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from a concurrent execution context like a child task.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Refer to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TaskGroup","type":"reference"},{"text":" documentation for detailed discussion of semantics shared between all task groups.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Discarding behavior","anchor":"Discarding-behavior"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A discarding task group eagerly discards and releases its child tasks as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"soon as they complete. This allows for the efficient releasing of memory used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by those tasks, which are not